# Docker & Compose

The **production** image (`docker/Dockerfile`) runs three roles via `SERVICE_ROLE`: **web**, **worker**, **beat**.

The **dev / CI** image (`docker/Dockerfile.dev`) installs **all** extras from `uv.lock` (pytest, ruff, mypy, Babel, …). It is used only as the Compose service `dev` in `docker-compose.test.yml` (`docker compose … run --rm dev <cmd>`). The repo is bind-mounted at `/workspace`; do not rely on baking application code into `Dockerfile.dev`.

## Dockerfile (multi-stage)

```dockerfile
# stage 1: build deps + compile gettext catalogs
FROM python:3.14-slim AS builder
ENV PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1
WORKDIR /app
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends build-essential libpq-dev && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock ./
RUN pip install --upgrade pip uv && uv sync --frozen --no-dev
COPY app/locales/ app/locales/
COPY babel.cfg .
RUN uv run pybabel compile -d app/locales/   # .po → .mo (deterministic per build)

# stage 2: runtime
FROM python:3.14-slim AS runtime
ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1
RUN groupadd -r app && useradd -r -g app -s /sbin/nologin app
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=builder /app/.venv /app/.venv
COPY --from=builder /app/app/locales/ /app/app/locales/   # compiled .mo
ENV PATH="/app/.venv/bin:$PATH"
COPY --chown=app:app . .
USER app
EXPOSE 8000
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s --start-period=20s --retries=3 \
  CMD curl -fsS http://localhost:8000/health || exit 1
ENTRYPOINT ["docker/entrypoint.sh"]
CMD []
```

## Hard rules

- ❌ NEVER run as root in the runtime stage.
- ❌ NEVER copy the entire repo before deps; cache the layer with `pyproject.toml` + lockfile first.
- ❌ NEVER bake secrets into the image (`.env`, keys). Pass at runtime.
- ❌ NEVER add `apt-get install` in the runtime stage without `--no-install-recommends` and cleanup.
- ❌ NEVER omit a healthcheck.
- ✅ Pin Python (`3.14-slim` not `3-slim`); pin base image digest in production.
- ✅ Image labels: `org.opencontainers.image.revision`, `version`, `source`.
- ✅ `.dockerignore` excludes `.git`, `tests/`, `docs/`, `*.md`, dotfiles.

## Entrypoint (selects role)

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
case "${SERVICE_ROLE:-web}" in
  web)    exec gunicorn app.main:app -k uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker -b 0.0.0.0:${PORT:-8000} \
            --workers "${GUNICORN_WORKERS:-3}" --timeout 60 --graceful-timeout 30 --keep-alive 5 --access-logfile - --error-logfile - ;;
  worker) exec celery -A app.workers.celery_app worker --loglevel=INFO --concurrency="${CELERY_WORKER_CONCURRENCY:-4}" -Q "${CELERY_QUEUES:-default,events}" ;;
  beat)   exec celery -A app.workers.celery_app beat --loglevel=INFO --scheduler "${CELERY_BEAT_SCHEDULER:-celery.beat.PersistentScheduler}" ;;
  *)      echo "Unknown SERVICE_ROLE: ${SERVICE_ROLE}"; exit 1 ;;
esac
```

## docker-compose.yml (dev)

- Services: `api`, `worker`, `beat`, `postgres`, `redis`, `mailpit`.
- All app services use the **same** image; differ only by `SERVICE_ROLE`.
- Use named volumes for `postgres_data`, `redis_data`.
- Healthchecks on `postgres` (`pg_isready`) and `redis` (`redis-cli ping`); app services `depends_on: { condition: service_healthy }`.
- Bind-mount `./app` for hot reload (dev only); not in prod images.

## docker-compose.test.yml (isolation)

- Services: `postgres_test` (port 55432), `redis_test` (port 56379), `mailpit_test`, **`dev`** (toolchain).
- Pytest, Alembic in CI, ruff, mypy, Babel, and drift scripts run **inside `dev`** with Compose network URLs (`postgres_test`, `redis_test`). **Do not** document host `pytest` as the supported path.
- Named volume `postgres_test_data` for Postgres data (ephemeral when using `make test-down` / `down -v`).
- Tests run via `make test` or `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml run --rm dev pytest …`. CI uses the same Compose file.

## Build & cache

- Use BuildKit (`DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1`).
- Cache to a registry in CI: `--cache-to type=registry,ref=...:cache --cache-from type=registry,ref=...:cache`.
- Tag images: `<repo>:<git-sha>` and `<repo>:latest` (latest only on main).

## Image scanning

- Trivy / Grype in CI; fail on **High** CVEs in app deps and base image.
- Re-pin base image when CVEs land; cron a weekly rebuild even when no app code changes.
